        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carroll County, Ohio\n- People: Charles Carroll of Carrollton, Doc Watson, Jeff Pfeffer, Bill Schardt, Jack Zalusky\n- Organizations: La Crosse Blackhawks\n- Topics: Declaration of Independence, Major League Baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the last surviving signer of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the only Catholic signatory of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Carroll County, Ohio, was named for Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Doc Watson was born in Carroll County, Ohio, on January 30, 1886.\n- Doc Watson was a pitcher in Major League Baseball.\n- Doc Watson died in San Diego, California, on December 30, 1949.\n- Jeff Pfeffer played for the La Crosse Blackhawks.\n- Bill Schardt played for the La Crosse Blackhawks.\n- Doc Watson played for the La Crosse Blackhawks.\n- Jack Zalusky played for the La Crosse Blackhawks.",
